# Build context filter for the headless game server image (Stage 2, task T50).
#
# Docker reads .dockerignore from the ROOT OF THE BUILD CONTEXT, which is why
# this file sits next to the Dockerfile: the main context of the reference build
# is this directory. The reference invocation is not repeated here -- it lives in
# the header of the Dockerfile, and from T51 on in build.sh, which is where it
# becomes executable rather than quoted.
#
# The file governs exactly the directory it lives in. Had the artifact
# directory been the main context instead, this file would have been ignored
# altogether -- it would not be at that context's root.
#
# The game artifact does not come through here at all: it arrives as the named
# context `game` and is filtered by the targeted COPY instructions in the
# Dockerfile, which do not depend on any ignore file.
#
# Deny everything, then allow the single file the image needs. Written this way
# round so that whatever lands in this directory later (build.sh in T51, notes,
# editor leftovers) stays out of the context without anyone remembering to add
# it here. The Dockerfile itself needs no exception: BuildKit loads the file
# named by `-f` outside this context, so the deny pattern below never applies
# to it.
*
!entrypoint.sh
